=============================================================================
Why GPL-3.0: transitive license obligations
=============================================================================

This project is a thin orchestration layer on top of four upstream libraries.
The resulting binary is a combined work; its license is the most restrictive
of its components:

    Component      License     Notes
    ------------   --------    -----------------------------------------------
    libigl v2.5.0  MPL-2.0     core / NRosy / MIQ wrapper. File-level copyleft.
    CoMISo         GPL-3.0     Mixed-integer QP solver. Transitive => GPL.
    libQEx         GPL-3.0     Quad mesh extractor (Ebke et al. 2013).
    OpenMesh       BSD-3       libQEx's only hard dependency.
    OpenBLAS       BSD-3       Runtime linear algebra (via vcpkg).
    Eigen          MPL-2.0     Header-only, transitive through libigl.
    GLFW / ImGui   zlib / MIT  Viewer only, permissive.

Because CoMISo and libQEx are GPL-3.0-or-later, any distributed binary that
links against them (statically or dynamically) must be released under GPL-3.0
as well. This project therefore adopts GPL-3.0 as its overall license.

If you want a more permissive license for downstream use, you must replace
both CoMISo and libQEx with non-GPL alternatives (e.g., port the mixed-integer
solver to Eigen's SparseQR + custom rounding, and implement your own quad
extractor). That's a substantial rewrite beyond the scope of this repository.


